From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Age of Decomp patch queue <aod-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:28:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aod: apply a colour profile chosen outside the game

The launcher and RecompLauncher write only the profile's name (color_preset),
but the picture read just the four values, so Vivid or Clarity picked there
changed nothing. The profiles now live in runtime/color_presets.h, shared by
the menu and the picture: a named profile sets the four values, custom keeps
the player's own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/color_presets.h           | 23 +++++++++++
 runtime/ui/menu.cpp               | 16 ++++----
 runtime/vk_color.c                | 14 ++++---
 tests/hwaoi/test_color_presets.py | 68 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 runtime/color_presets.h
 create mode 100644 tests/hwaoi/test_color_presets.py

diff --git a/runtime/color_presets.h b/runtime/color_presets.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0e42ada4218345c05eed7f512620bdbbcff06b9d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/runtime/color_presets.h
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+// The colour profiles of the in-game menu (ui/menu.cpp) and of the launcher's "Colour" setting, which writes only the
+// profile's name to hwaoi.ini. The picture (vk_color.c) takes a named profile's four values from this table; only
+// "custom" uses COLOR_BRIGHTNESS/CONTRAST/SATURATION/GAMMA as the player set them.
+#pragma once
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+typedef struct {
+    const char *name, *brightness, *contrast, *saturation, *gamma;
+} ColorPreset;
+
+static const ColorPreset color_presets[] = {
+    {"default", "0", "100", "100", "1"},
+    {"vivid", "0", "115", "135", "0.95"},
+    {"clarity", "2", "110", "115", "1"},
+};
+
+// The named profile, or NULL for "custom" and any other name: the four values are then the player's own.
+static inline const ColorPreset *color_preset_find(const char *name) {
+    for (size_t i = 0; name && i < sizeof color_presets / sizeof *color_presets; i++)
+        if (!strcmp(name, color_presets[i].name)) return &color_presets[i];
+    return NULL;
+}
